# Everything the build and the packaging scripts produce lands under target/:
# cargo's own output, cargo-deb's tree, the AppImage AppDir, the flatpak-builder
# state and repo, the snap's staged copy of the sources, and every finished
# artifact (.deb, .AppImage, .flatpak, .snap, .zip). One line covers all of it,
# and `make clean` removes it too.
/target

# flatpak-builder's default state directory, created when a build runs without
# packaging/build-flatpak.sh (which points it at target/flatpak instead).
/.flatpak-builder

# Freebuff's per-project marker: tool state, never source.
/.freebuff

# appimagetool, downloaded into the checkout as packaging/build-appimage.sh's
# error message suggests when it is not already on PATH.
/appimagetool

# Rust leaves these behind when an interrupted build or an editor save breaks
# the tree.
**/*.rs.bk

# Editor and OS scratch.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Scratch images: screenshots and downloads are not source. Two kinds of PNG
# are, and both are included by path, so an ignored file cannot break a build
# after a fresh clone:
#   - the 256x256 icon that cargo-deb, the AppImage, the snap and the Flatpak
#     each read from the tree;
#   - captured test pictures, which tests pull in with include_bytes!.
*.png
!packaging/icons/*.png
!fixtures/**/*.png
